  "id": "majority-influence",
  "term": "majority influence",
  "definition": "Majority influence is a form of social influence in which a person’s judgment or choice is shaped by the apparent opinion of most other people. In the source context, it refers to conformity prompted by the balance of positive versus negative comments or reviews.",
